# 📘 **UI Requirements Document – Storefront Admin UI**

## 🧾 Overview

The Storefront Admin UI is a centralized admin panel for internal IT and procurement teams to view, control, and manage all aspects of the Storefront system, including user device inventory, request tracking, Slack-based approval workflows, device analytics, and inventory management.

---

## 🧱 Page-Level UI Requirements

### 1. **User Device Inventory Search**

* **Page Title**: User Inventory Search

* **Purpose**: Search and view current user-to-device assignments

* **UI Components**:

  * **Search Filters** (Multi-field):

    * Email ID (text input)
    * Device Name (dropdown or auto-complete)
    * Serial Number (text input)
    * Lease End Date (date picker)
    * End of Life Date (date picker)
  * **Search Button**
  * **Results Table**:

    * Columns: Email, Device Name, Serial Number, Lease End, EOL Date, Status
    * Pagination
    * Export to CSV (optional)

* **Interactions**:

  * Search triggers API call to fetch matched records
  * Filters are optional but combinable
  * Clicking a record could open a side panel for more details (optional)

---

### 2. **Storefront Request Search**

* **Page Title**: Request Search

* **Purpose**: Track device requests submitted by users

* **UI Components**:

  * **Search Filters**:

    * Reference Number (text input)
    * Email Address (text input)
    * Requested Device Type (dropdown)
    * Requested Date (range date picker)
  * **Search Button**
  * **Results Table**:

    * Columns: Ref ID, Email, Device Type, Requested Date, Status
    * Actions: View Request Details (button/icon)
    * Pagination

* **Interactions**:

  * Results are shown in table format
  * Export option for results
  * Filter state should persist during navigation (optional)

---

### 3. **Slack Approval Toggle Controls**

* **Page Title**: Slack Approval Settings

* **Purpose**: Enable or disable Slack-based approval by department or user type

* **UI Components**:

  * **Toggle Switch List**:

    * Label: Department/Group Name (e.g., Technology, HR, Finance)
    * Switch Component: On/Off
    * Description or Tooltip for each row explaining the behavior
  * **Save Changes** Button

* **Interactions**:

  * Each toggle change is saved after clicking Save
  * Can be extended to support rule-based toggles (e.g., auto-approve for test devices)

---

### 4. **Device Trend & Analytics Dashboard**

* **Page Title**: Analytics Dashboard

* **Purpose**: Show visual representation of device request patterns and department usage

* **UI Components**:

  * **Small Cards / Widgets** (top-level metrics):

    * Total Requests Today
    * Total Approved
    * Pending Requests
  * **Bar Chart**: Requests per Day (X: Date, Y: Number of Requests)
  * **Pie Chart**: Mac vs Windows
  * **Horizontal Bar Chart**: Requests by Department
  * **Filter Panel** (optional): Date Range Picker, Department

* **Interactions**:

  * Responsive widgets
  * Hover tooltips on charts
  * Filterable data views

---

### 5. **Inventory Dashboard**

* **Page Title**: Inventory Overview

* **Purpose**: Display current inventory of devices and peripherals

* **UI Components**:

  * **Filter Panel**:

    * Device Type (Laptop/Peripheral dropdown)
    * OS Type (Mac/Windows dropdown)
    * Availability (Available / Unavailable / In Use)
  * **Summary Cards**:

    * Total Available Devices
    * Total In Use
    * Peripheral Count
  * **Inventory Table**:

    * Columns: Device Type, Model, Status, Last Updated
    * Tag/Badge for status
    * Pagination

* **Interactions**:

  * Dropdown filters trigger re-rendering of inventory list
  * Status shown as colored badges (green: available, red: unavailable, grey: in use)

---

### 6. **Device & Peripheral Management (Add/Update)**

* **Page Title**: Device Management

* **Purpose**: Admins can add new devices or update status of existing ones

* **UI Components**:

  * **Form Section – Add New Device**:

    * Device Type: Dropdown (Laptop / Peripheral)
    * OS Type: Dropdown (Mac / Windows / Other)
    * Device Model: Dropdown (Pre-defined or free text)
    * User Profile Type: Dropdown (Executive / Standard / Performance)
    * Serial Number (optional)
    * Status Toggle (Available / Unavailable)
    * Submit Button
  * **Form Section – Update Existing**:

    * Select device by serial or device ID
    * Editable fields: Status, Assigned Profile
    * Save Changes Button

* **Interactions**:

  * Forms should have validation (e.g., required fields, dropdown dependencies)
  * Confirmation modals before saving changes
  * Show success or error toasts

---

## 📌 General UI/UX Considerations

* **Design System**: Preferably align with existing internal design system (GEICO theme or Material UI if none)
* **Navigation**:

  * Sidebar-based navigation or top-tab layout for sections
* **Responsiveness**:

  * Must work on desktop; mobile support is optional
* **Loading States**:

  * Show skeleton loaders or spinners on data-heavy components
* **Error Handling**:

  * Friendly error messages for empty results or server errors
* **Permissions**:

  * Hide or disable sensitive controls based on role (optional)

---

## 🔍 Suggested Component Libraries

* React-based: Material UI, Ant Design, or Chakra UI
* Charting: Recharts / Chart.js / ApexCharts
* Date Pickers: React-DateRange or Material Date Pickers

